      "evidence": "Transcribed from the two statutory designation notices published by Burnley Borough Council: 'Burnley Wood with Healey Wood 2022-2027' (https://burnley.gov.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Burnley-Wood-Healey-Wood-2022.pdf, 22 streets) and 'Leyland Road 2022-2027' (https://burnley.gov.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Leyland-Road-2022.pdf, 21 streets); both notices record the designation as made 19 January 2022, confirmed by the Secretary of State 21 April 2022, in force 21 July 2022 to 20 July 2027. Every street name and number restriction was independently cross-checked against the council's combined 'All areas street list 2025' PDF (https://burnley.gov.uk/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/All-areas-street-list-2025.pdf), which tags each street with its area, and the two sources agree exactly with no additions, omissions or differing ranges. In these notices the number restriction is printed in the column to the LEFT of the street name; that column order was confirmed by the all-areas PDF, whose labelled 'Street'/'Area' header shows the same pairings. 'Springhill Road.' carries a trailing full stop in the council's own document and is reproduced verbatim; en dashes in ranges are rendered as hyphens."
