      "evidence": "Transcribed from Burnley Borough Council's official 'All areas street list 2025' PDF, linked as 'All areas street list 2025' from https://burnley.gov.uk/housing/private-rented-sector/selective-licensing/. The PDF is a three-column table (property numbers | Street | Area); only rows tagged Trinity, Queensgate, Gannow, Daneshouse or Padiham are included here and the Burnleywood and Leyland Road rows (the 2022-2027 scheme) were excluded. Source row counts by area: Daneshouse 65, Queensgate 68, Trinity 56, Padiham 52, Gannow 40. The Daneshouse rows were independently verified against the council's separate designation notice (https://burnley.gov.uk/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Notice-of-Notification-Daneshouse-Stoneyholme-2025-2030.pdf), which uses the same numbers-then-street column order. Street names keep the council's own capitalisation (Daneshouse rows are printed in upper case in the source). Several streets appear more than once with different ranges (e.g. Briercliffe Road, Lionel Street, Padiham Road, Carter Street); these are separate rows in the council's list and are preserved as separate entries. One row is tagged 'Queensgtae', an obvious typo for Queensgate in the source, and has been treated as Queensgate. The final two Daneshouse entries, '1 and 2 Poplar House' and 'Emmaus House (all)', are printed by the council in the numbers column with no street-name value and are transcribed verbatim as printed. Note that the Gannow, Padiham, Queensgate and Trinity designation notices are hosted on a Burnley Council SharePoint site rather than on burnley.gov.uk, so this council-published street list is used as the source."
